8/22/2026 Todd Carnes <toddcarnes@gmail.com> (SDLHana 1.0.0 released):
 * In-Game Scrollable Rules Viewer: Replaced legacy 4-page rules screen with a smooth offscreen canvas rules viewer (RulesMenu()) displaying 100% of the text, month-by-month card breakdowns, Yaku combinations, and card sprite illustrations from RULES.md across a maximized 545px viewport.
 * Interactive Scrollbar Dragging & Multi-Input Controls: Implemented interactive scrollbar thumb dragging (SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION), high-precision mouse wheel scrolling (SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_WHEEL float processing), keyboard arrow navigation (SDLK_UP / SDLK_DOWN), and viewport click-scrolling.
 * Surface Clipping & Typography Refinements: Applied strict surface clipping (SDL_SetSurfaceClipRect) around the rules viewport container to eliminate border overbleed, updated 2D text centering in DrawTextInBox, and set header title typography to dark navy blue (20, 32, 52) on teal background for high contrast and legibility.
 * Traditional Dealer Selection: Implemented authentic Hanafuda dealer selection rules. Round 1 uses a traditional Mekuri card draw cut animation where both players draw a random card from the deck, selecting the player with the lowest month card as the first dealer (Oya / Sun). Subsequent rounds retain the winner of the previous round as dealer (or retain current dealer on draws).
 * Graphics & Flicker Elimination: Removed premature UpdateScreen calls inside CGeneral::ClearScreen and AnimCardMove, preserving actual underlying table pixels in animation buffer surfaces to eliminate screen flickering and black flashes on card selection.
 * Dynamic UI Text Centering: Implemented CGeneral::DrawTextInBox to dynamically center TTF font text within bounding boxes, resolving descender clipping on all UI prompt boxes, main menu buttons, and dialogs across English, French, Japanese, and Simplified Chinese.
 * Window Resizability & Logical Presentation: Set default window size to 1024x768 with SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE and configured SDL_SetRenderLogicalPresentation with SDL_ConvertEventToRenderCoordinates to enable crisp full-window stretching and accurate mouse interaction across high-DPI displays while defaulting to windowed mode on launch.
 * Redesigned Action Dialogs: Expanded "Would you like to continue the game?" (WantToContinue) and "Double Up" dialog boxes to 100px height with styled blue/red action buttons and centered text.
 * Comprehensive Documentation: Created illustrated RULES.md repository guide detailing Hanafuda deck structure, Mekuri dealer selection, Koi-Koi Yaku sets, Korean Go-Stop scoring/penalties, and Bet Mode. Updated README.md with Authentic Game Mechanics feature section.

8/21/2026 Todd Carnes <toddcarnes@gmail.com>:
 * Game Loop & Victory Condition: Transformed endless round loop into a structured 12-round Hanafuda match (January through December). Added round HUD indicator (RD X/12) and implemented final ShowMatchResults() victory/defeat screen displaying final match score and sound effects before returning to the Main Menu.
 * Graphics Engine: Upgraded card asset pipeline to high-definition vector Hanafuda cardset derived from Wikimedia Commons (Category:SVG_Hanafuda_with_traditional_colors_(black_border)). Preserved authentic black hill on August Moon, vibrant traditional inks, crisp black card borders, and classic red card backs. Stored individual 300 DPI vector source card tiles in tools/cards_trad/.
 * macOS Packaging: Configured native MACOSX_BUNDLE target properties in CMakeLists.txt (SDLHana.app) with automatic .icns icon generation (sips / iconutil). Updated release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml) to package self-contained SDLHana.app bundles for macOS users.
 * Organization Namespace: Updated SDL_GetPrefPath organization name to "CarneSoft" in src/main.cpp and macOS bundle GUI identifier to "com.carnesoft.sdlhana" in CMakeLists.txt.
 * Release Automation: Created GitHub Actions release deployment workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml) to automatically package and attach self-contained game bundles (Windows .zip, macOS .tar.gz, Linux .tar.gz) on release tag publication.
 * Continuous Integration: Separated build CI into per-OS workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml, build-macos.yml, build-linux.yml) with live status badges on README.md.
 * Application Icon: Appended src/sdlhana.rc to Windows executable target for native Windows Explorer icon embedding and implemented cross-platform SetAppWindowIcon() using SDL_SetWindowIcon() and sdlhana.xpm.
 * Game Engine Fixes: Reset m_iScore to 0 in InitGame() to prevent score leaking across game sessions, and isolated Korean-specific "Leave Three" scoring rules to GAMEMODE_KOREAN.
 * Developer Tools: Created tools/CMakeLists.txt with optional SDLHANA_BUILD_TOOLS CMake build flag for title2cl, removing legacy Autotools Makefiles and #ifdef WITH_CONFIG_H blocks.
 * Documentation: Updated README.md with Game Modes, Supported Languages (without emojis), and GNU Savannah project attribution.

8/20/2026 Todd Carnes <toddcarnes@gmail.com>:
 * Build System: Replaced legacy autotools/VC++6 .dsp scripts with modern CMake 3.25+ (CMakeLists.txt) supporting Windows 11 (Visual Studio 2026 MSVC), macOS (Clang), and Linux (GCC).
 * Graphics Engine: Migrated rendering pipeline from legacy software SDL_Surface CPU blitting to native hardware-accelerated SDL3 (SDL_Window*, SDL_Renderer*, SDL_Texture*). Added letterboxed 640x480 logical presentation canvas and coordinate mapping for windowed and fullscreen modes (SDL_RenderCoordinatesFromWindow).
 * Audio Engine: Refactored audio handling from low-level PCM audio stream conversion to native SDL3_mixer (MIX_Init, MIX_CreateMixerDevice, MIX_LoadAudio, MIX_PlayAudio).
 * Font Engine: Upgraded CFont into a hybrid font renderer supporting vector TrueType/OpenType fonts via SDL3_ttf with INI configuration (UseTTF=1, TTFFontPath=...) while preserving 100% fallback support for original 2005 compressed .fnt bitmap fonts (eng.fnt, fra.fnt, chs.fnt, jpn.fnt).
 * State & File System: Encapsulated loose global pointers into a unified Application context singleton. Modernized save/config handling to use SDL_GetPrefPath() and std::filesystem::path for cross-platform preference storage.
 * C++23 Modernization: Refactored raw memory management to std::unique_ptr and stack RAII, modernized C-string/printf formatting with std::println and <print>, and updated random number generation with <random> (std::mt19937).
 * Continuous Integration: Created GitHub Actions matrix workflow (.github/workflows/build.yml) automating build validation on Windows, macOS, and Linux runners.

